Problem: Given point \( O \) inside triangle \( \triangle ABC \), such that \( \overrightarrow{OA} + 2 \overrightarrow{OB} + 3 \overrightarrow{OC} = \overrightarrow{0} \), what is the ratio of the area of \( \triangle ABC \) to the area of \( \triangle AOC \)?
(A) 2
(B) \(\frac{3}{2}\)
(C) 3
(D) \(\frac{5}{3}\)

Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{}.<|im_end|>
